@jul22_index
title: Demand indexed wages, pensions and public contracts
subtitle: Protect incomes openly and accept the fiscal fight attached to automatic adjustment.
on-arrival: household_policy_pressure += 5; labor_credibility += 5; public_sector_support += 3; budget_promises += 3; left_economic_position -= 4; economic_issue_salience += 2; tactical_desertion_to_abstention += 0.4; last_policy_stage = "Proposal"; last_policy_authority = "Parliamentary opposition"; last_policy_implementation = 0; news_headline = "The Left makes indexation the answer to inflation"

Teachers, nurses, pensioners and local contractors receive one rule: public
commitments should rise before inflation quietly cuts them. Unions can organise
around a number instead of waiting for discretionary relief.

The proposal is expensive and gives opponents an easy headline about a wage-
price spiral. Lewica has chosen visible household protection and must now defend
its cost.

- @poland_event_queue: Continue


@jul22_tax
title: Lead with a simple technical tax correction
subtitle: Win back people hit by payroll chaos while leaving the distributional loss less answered.
on-arrival: public_trust += 1; liberal_professionals_left_affinity += 2; left_economic_position += 4; labor_dissent += 3; razem_dissent += 4; ko_economic_position += 2; tactical_desertion_to_ko += 1; news_headline = "Tax competence replaces another grand promise"

Accountants and professional associations help us reduce the next correction
to rules employers and workers can actually calculate. The competence argument
reaches people who stopped listening after January's contradictory guidance.

It does less for wages already losing purchasing power. KO finds the proposal
easy to adopt, while unions and Razem ask why technical simplicity became the
Left's principal answer to a distributional crisis.

- @poland_event_queue: Continue


@jul22_investment
title: Make courts and KPO investment the anti-inflation package
subtitle: Connect legal repair to supply and public investment, accepting a slower household answer.
on-arrival: kpo_scrutiny += 2; judicial_legitimacy += 3; ko_relation += 3; household_policy_pressure += 1; public_trust += 1; tactical_desertion_to_ko += 0.8; last_policy_stage = "Advocacy"; last_policy_authority = "Parliamentary opposition"; last_policy_implementation = 0; news_headline = "Frozen investment and broken courts become one economic case"

Lewica takes stalled municipal projects to the court debate and argues that
institutional repair has a price visible in housing, energy and transport.
KO joins the case, and “rule of law” acquires something more concrete than a
Brussels press conference.

The link is real but delayed. A household opening this month's bill cannot
spend a future KPO project, so the party still lacks an immediate income shield.

- @poland_event_queue: Continue

@jul22_supply
title: Freeze regulation and cut employer charges to expand supply
subtitle: A market answer to inflation strengthens capitalist organisers and deepens left-caucus dissent.
on-arrival: left_economic_position += 7; left_right_score += 5; market_liberal_support += 10; liberal_professionals_left_affinity += 3; public_trust += 1; barons_dissent -= 2; labor_dissent += 9; razem_dissent += 10; progressives_dissent += 4; household_policy_pressure -= 3; konf_poll_momentum -= 0.1; news_headline = "Lewica answers inflation with a supply-side turn"

Employer groups and some self-employed professionals welcome a pause in rules
and lower charges. Lewica briefly occupies economic ground Konfederacja assumed
belonged to it alone.

The turn asks workers to wait for cheaper supply while their protections and
public revenue are reduced now. Labour and Razem organise against their own
party's answer, and the radical right claims vindication for setting the terms.

- @poland_event_queue: Continue
